(* ============================================================================
   EBNF PRIMER (READ THIS FIRST)
   ============================================================================

   This file is an EBNF “data dictionary” that describes the JSON request bodies
   for the C2M Jobs submission endpoints:

     POST /static
     POST /static/multi    [PLANNED — not yet implemented; multiDocJobs/multiDocJobItem schemas are reserved]
     POST /static/address-capture
     POST /mail-merge
     POST /batch/split
     POST /batch/split/address-capture
     POST /batch/zip
     POST /batch/zip/address-capture

   If you have never seen EBNF before, think of it as a compact way to describe
   “what fields can appear” and “how those fields can be combined”.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1) Big picture: how this file is used
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   - EBNF is the SOURCE OF TRUTH in the pipeline.
   - A translator converts this EBNF into an OpenAPI (YAML) specification.
   - The generated OpenAPI can then be imported into tools like Postman and used
     to generate tests once examples are added.

   So the EBNF defines structure; OpenAPI is a generated artifact.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2) What a rule is
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   A rule looks like:

     ruleName = something ;

   - 'ruleName' is the name of the concept being defined.
   - '=' means “is defined as”.
   - ';' ends the rule.

   Example:
     id = integer ;

   Means: wherever 'id' is used, it is an integer.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3) How we represent JSON objects in this dialect
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This file follows the style used by the existing (old) data dictionary that
   your CI/CD translator already understands:

   - We do NOT write literal JSON punctuation (no '{', '}', ':', or quoted field
     names).
   - Instead, each JSON “field” is modeled as its own rule (e.g., address1),
     and objects are modeled by combining fields with '+'.

   Example:
     returnAddress = firstName + lastName + address1 + city + state + zip + country ;

   Read as: returnAddress contains firstName, lastName, address1, city, state, zip, country.

   Important: the EBNF describes the set/shape of fields, while the generated
   OpenAPI expresses them as JSON object properties.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   4) Combining fields with '+'
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   In this data dictionary:

     A + B + C

   Means: the object contains A, B, and C.

   This is object “composition” (think: required fields) rather than arithmetic.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   5) Optional fields: [ ... ]
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Square brackets mean OPTIONAL.

     [ foo ]

   Means: foo may appear, or it may be omitted.

   Example:
     requestIdSource = requestId + [ filename ] ;

   Read as: requestIdSource must include requestId, and may include filename.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   6) Alternatives: A | B
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The vertical bar means "one of these alternatives".

     docSourceStandard = documentIdSource | requestIdSource | urlSource ;

   Read as: docSourceStandard can be provided in exactly one of these modes.

   In OpenAPI this often becomes a 'oneOf' (depending on translator behavior).

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   7) Repetition / arrays: { ... }
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Curly braces mean repetition (zero or more) in standard EBNF.

     { item }

   Means: 0..N occurrences of item.
   In JSON terms, we use this to represent arrays/lists.

   Example:
     addressList = { address } ;

   Read as: addressList is a list of addresses.

   Note: This dialect typically does not encode “at least one” (1..N) directly.
   If the API requires at least one entry, that constraint is enforced by:
   - API validation, and/or
   - additional OpenAPI constraints (minItems), if your translator supports them.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   8) Endpoint request bodies: submit...Params
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Each endpoint has a rule named like:

     submitSingleDocParams = ... ;

   This rule defines the JSON body shape for that endpoint. It is built from the
   shared building blocks (docSourceAll, recipientAddressSource, etc.).

   Example:
     submitSingleDocParams =
           [ jobTemplate ]
         + docSourceAll
         + recipientAddressSource
         + [ paymentDetails ]
         + ... ;

   Read as: the request body includes the required parts, plus optional parts.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   9) Primitive types used here
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   - string  : a JSON string
   - integer : a JSON integer
   - id      : an alias for integer, used when the integer is an ID

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   10) What EBNF does NOT capture by itself
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   EBNF is great at describing structure, but some business rules are not fully
   represented here (or may not be representable in your translator), such as:
   - “filename is required only if multiple files were uploaded”
   - “jobs[] must have at least one element”
   - “for endpoint X, recipientAddressSource must be present/absent”
   Those are enforced by endpoint-level rules and server-side validation, and
   can also be expressed in OpenAPI once examples/constraints are added.

   ============================================================================ *)


(* C2M Jobs Submission API - Data Dictionary (EBNF)
   Source: Data lead proposal (Dec 02 2025) for C2M Jobs submission endpoints.
   Purpose: EBNF is the source of truth; EBNF -> OpenAPI (YAML) is generated in CI/CD.

   This file is intentionally written to match the EBNF style used in c2mapiv2-dd.ebnf (old endpoints):
     - rules use '='
     - object composition uses '+'
     - optional fields use '[ ... ]'
     - arrays use '{ ... }'
     - rules terminate with ';'

   Conventions:
     - Endpoint param sets (submit...Params) represent the JSON request body shape for that endpoint.
     - Each 'Params' rule is composed from reusable building blocks (document source variants, recipientAddressSource, etc.).
     - Optional fields are wrapped in [ ... ].
     - Arrays are represented as { item }.
*)


(***********************************)
(*        ENDPOINT DEFINITIONS      *)
(***********************************)

(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* Endpoint: POST /static                                                              *)
(* @summary Submit single document *)
(* @description Submits a mailing job for a single document to one or more recipients. The request body must include a document source, recipient address information, and payment details. *)
(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)

(* English meaning:
   - Body MAY include jobTemplate (preferred options selector).
   - Body MUST include `docSourceAll` (document source).
     `docSourceAll` can be:
       - documentIdSource (documentId): References a stored document by ID
       - requestIdSource (requestId + [filename]): References an uploaded file from a previous upload request
       - urlSource (url): URL to fetch document from external source
       - zipDocumentIdSource (zipDocumentId + filename): References a file within a stored zip archive
       - zipRequestIdSource (requestId + zipFilename + filename): References a file within an uploaded zip archive

     *** Mahesh: Can this endpoint be called with zipDocumentIdSource and zipRequestIdSource??

   - Body MUST include recipientAddressSource (single address OR list OR stored list).
     recipientAddressSource can be:
       - (mappingId + singleAddress [+addressName]): Single recipient with mapping
       - (mappingId + addressList [+addressListName]): List of recipients with mapping
       - addressListId: Reference to stored address list
     Note: mappingId is optional. If omitted, the server will use the default mapping ID.
   - Body MAY include paymentDetails, returnAddress, jobOptions, tags.
*)

(* Decision / validation rules (implementation-required):
   Document source (docSourceAll):
     IF docSourceAll is documentIdSource (documentId)
       THEN resolve stored document by documentId.
     ELSE IF docSourceAll is requestIdSource (requestId [+filename])
       THEN lookup upload request by requestId.
            IF upload request contains > 1 file
              THEN filename MUST be provided and MUST match a file in that request.
            ELSE filename MAY be omitted.
     ELSE IF docSourceAll is urlSource (url)
       THEN fetch document from url; reject if fetch fails or content-type not allowed.
     ELSE IF docSourceAll is zipDocumentIdSource (zipDocumentId + filename)
       THEN resolve zip archive by zipDocumentId; filename MUST exist in zip.
     ELSE IF docSourceAll is zipRequestIdSource (requestId + zipFilename + filename)
       THEN resolve upload request by requestId; zipFilename MUST identify the uploaded zip;
            filename MUST exist in that zip.
     ELSE reject (no supported docSourceAll variant).

   Recipient source (recipientAddressSource):
     IF recipientAddressSource is addressListId
       THEN load stored list by addressListId.
     ELSE IF recipientAddressSource is ([mappingId] + singleAddress [+addressName])
       THEN treat as single-recipient source; validate required address fields per product rules.
            IF mappingId is omitted
              THEN use server default mapping ID for merge-variable mapping.
            ELSE apply provided mappingId for merge-variable mapping.
     ELSE IF recipientAddressSource is ([mappingId] + addressList [+addressListName])
       THEN validate addressList has >= 1 entry.
            IF mappingId is omitted
              THEN use server default mapping ID for merge-variable mapping.
            ELSE apply provided mappingId for merge-variable mapping.
     ELSE reject (no supported recipientAddressSource variant).

   jobTemplate vs jobOptions:
     IF jobTemplate is present AND jobOptions is present
       THEN enforce policy (recommended: reject as mutually exclusive to avoid ambiguity).
     ELSE IF jobTemplate absent AND jobOptions absent
       THEN enforce defaults or reject (policy decision).

   Payment:
     IF paymentDetails present
       THEN exactly one payment variant must be used.
            ApplePay / GooglePay variants are excluded for initial testing (commented out).
*)

submitDocParams =
      [ jobTemplate ]
    + docSourceAll
    + recipientAddressSource
    + [ paymentDetails ]
    + [ returnAddress ]
    + [ jobOptions ]
    + [ tags ] ;

(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* Endpoint: POST /static/address-capture                                              *)
(* @summary Submit single document — address capture *)
(* @description Submits a mailing job for a single PDF where recipient addresses are captured from the document via OCR. No inline recipient address is required. *)
(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)

(* English meaning:
   - Body MAY include jobTemplate.
   - Body MUST include `docSourceStandard` (document source - non-zip variants only).
     `docSourceStandard` can be: documentIdSource, requestIdSource, or urlSource (zip sources not allowed for this endpoint).
   - Body MAY include paymentDetails, returnAddress, jobOptions, tags.
   - Body does NOT include recipientAddressSource because addresses are captured
     via OCR/address extraction workflow after document upload, not provided in request body.
*)

(* Decision / validation rules (implementation-required):
   Address capture constraint:
     IF request body includes recipientAddressSource (directly or nested)
       THEN reject (this endpoint relies on address capture workflow, not inline addresses).

   Document source:
     Apply the same docSourceStandard resolution rules as /static.

   Job list constraint:
     IF request body includes jobs
       THEN reject (this endpoint is not a split/bulk endpoint).

   jobTemplate vs jobOptions:
     Apply the same mutual-exclusion/default policy as /static.

   Payment:
     Same paymentDetails rules as /static (Apple/Google excluded).
*)

submitSinglePdfAddressCaptureParams =
      [ jobTemplate ]
    + docSourceStandard
    + [ paymentDetails ]
    + [ returnAddress ]
    + [ jobOptions ]
    + [ tags ] ;


(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* Endpoint: POST /batch/split                                                          *)
(* @summary Submit PDF split *)
(* @description Splits a single PDF into page ranges and mails each range to a different recipient. Each job item specifies page range and recipient address. *)
(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)

(* English meaning:
   - Body MAY include jobTemplate.
   - Body MUST include `docSourceStandard` (the PDF to split).
   - Body MUST include `pdfSplitJobsWithAddress` (list of page ranges with recipient addresses).
   - Each `pdfSplitJobsWithAddress[]` entry is a `pdfSplitJobItemWithAddress` containing:
       startPage (integer) + endPage (integer) + recipientAddressSource (address reference)
   - Body MAY include paymentDetails, returnAddress, jobOptions, tags.
*)

(* Decision / validation rules (implementation-required):
   Document type constraint:
     Resolve docSourceStandard.
     IF resolved document is not a PDF
       THEN reject.

   pdfSplitJobsWithAddress constraint:
     IF pdfSplitJobsWithAddress missing OR pdfSplitJobsWithAddress has 0 entries
       THEN reject.

   Per job item constraint:
     FOR EACH pdfSplitJobsWithAddress[i]:
       IF pdfSplitJobsWithAddress[i] is not a pdfSplitJobItemWithAddress shape
         THEN reject (only pdfSplitJobItemWithAddress allowed; multiDocJobItem and pdfSplitJobItemNoAddress not allowed).
       IF startPage missing OR endPage missing
         THEN reject.
       IF startPage < 1 OR endPage < 1
         THEN reject.
       IF startPage > endPage
         THEN reject.
       IF recipientAddressSource missing
         THEN reject (required for /batch/split).
*)

submitSinglePdfSplitParams =
      [ jobTemplate ]
    + docSourceStandard   (* choose, see below *)
    + pdfSplitJobsWithAddress
    + [ paymentDetails ]
    + [ returnAddress ]
    + [ jobOptions ]
    + [ tags ] ;


(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* Endpoint: POST /batch/split/address-capture                                          *)
(* @summary Submit PDF split — address capture *)
(* @description Splits a single PDF into page ranges where recipient addresses are captured from the PDF. No inline recipient addresses are required. *)
(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)

(* English meaning:
   - Same as /single/pdf/split, but recipient addresses are captured externally.
   - Body MAY include jobTemplate.
   - Body MUST include `docSourceStandard`.
   - Body MUST include `pdfSplitJobsNoAddress` (list of page ranges without addresses).
   - Each `pdfSplitJobsNoAddress[]` entry is a `pdfSplitJobItemNoAddress` containing:
       startPage (integer) + endPage (integer)
   - Body MAY include paymentDetails, returnAddress, jobOptions, tags.

   Implementation note:
   - This DD models pdfSplitJobItem with [ recipientAddressSource ] (optional).
     Endpoint-level validation differentiates required/omitted usage per path.
*)

(* Decision / validation rules (implementation-required):
   Document type constraint:
     Resolve docSourceStandard.
     IF resolved document is not a PDF
       THEN reject.

   pdfSplitJobsNoAddress constraint:
     IF pdfSplitJobsNoAddress missing OR pdfSplitJobsNoAddress has 0 entries
       THEN reject.

   Per job item constraint:
     FOR EACH pdfSplitJobsNoAddress[i]:
       IF pdfSplitJobsNoAddress[i] is not a pdfSplitJobItemNoAddress shape
         THEN reject.
       Validate startPage/endPage same as /batch/split.
       IF recipientAddressSource is present
         THEN reject (addresses must be captured externally for this endpoint).
*)

submitSinglePdfSplitAddressCaptureParams =
      [ jobTemplate ]
    + docSourceStandard
    + pdfSplitJobsNoAddress
    + [ paymentDetails ]
    + [ returnAddress ]
    + [ jobOptions ]
    + [ tags ] ;

(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* Endpoint: POST /mail-merge                                                           *)
(* @summary Submit mail merge *)
(* @description Merges multiple documents into a single mailing sent to one recipient. Useful for creating document packets or multi-page letters. *)
(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)

(* English meaning:
   - Merges multiple documents then submits the merged result as one job.
   - Body MAY include jobTemplate.
   - Body MUST include mergeDocumentSource (documentsToMerge[]).
   - Body MUST include recipientAddressSource.
   - Body MAY include paymentDetails, returnAddress, jobOptions, tags.
*)

(* Decision / validation rules (implementation-required):
   Merge list constraint:
     IF documentsToMerge missing OR documentsToMerge has 0 entries
       THEN reject.
     (Recommended) IF documentsToMerge has 1 entry
       THEN reject or treat as non-merge (policy decision; recommend reject to avoid confusion).

   Per merge ref:
     FOR EACH mergeDocumentRef in documentsToMerge:
       IF mergeDocumentRef is documentId
         THEN resolve stored document.
       ELSE IF mergeDocumentRef is requestId [+filename]
         THEN apply multi-file rule: filename required when upload request has >1 file.
       ELSE reject.

   Output constraint:
     IF merged output exceeds size/page limits
       THEN reject.

   Recipient:
     recipientAddressSource is REQUIRED and must resolve using /single/doc rules.
*)

submitMultiDocMergeParams =
      [ jobTemplate ]
    + mergeDocumentSource
    + recipientAddressSource
    + [ paymentDetails ]
    + [ returnAddress ]
    + [ jobOptions ]
    + [ tags ] ;


(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* Endpoint: POST /batch/zip                                                            *)
(* @summary Submit ZIP batch *)
(* @description Submits multiple mailing jobs sourced from files inside a single ZIP archive. Each job item specifies which file within the ZIP and the recipient address. *)
(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)

(* English meaning:
   - Submits multiple jobs from a single ZIP file.
   - Body MUST include docSourceZipFileRef (specifies which zip file - requestId or documentId only, no filename).
   - Body MUST include `multiZipJobs` (list of job items).
   - Each `multiZipJobs[]` item is a `multiZipJobItem` containing:
       [ jobTemplate ] + filename + recipientAddressSource
   - Each job can have its own jobTemplate, specifies which file within the zip, and recipient address.
   - Body MAY include paymentDetails and tags.
*)

(* Decision / validation rules (implementation-required):
   multiZipJobs constraint:
     IF multiZipJobs missing OR multiZipJobs has 0 entries
       THEN reject.

   Allowed job item shape:
     FOR EACH multiZipJobs[i]:
       IF multiZipJobs[i] is not a multiZipJobItem shape
         THEN reject.

   Zip policy:
     This endpoint is modeled as ZIP-ONLY in the grammar via:
       submitMultiZipParams requires docSourceZipFileRef (zip file reference at top-level)
       multiZipJobItem = [ jobTemplate ] + filename + recipientAddressSource ;

     The zip file is specified once at top-level via docSourceZipFileRef:
       - zipDocumentIdOnly (documentId only, no filename), OR
       - zipRequestIdOnly (requestId only, no filename)
     Each job item then specifies:
       - Optional jobTemplate (or inherits default if not specified)
       - filename (which file within the zip)
       - recipientAddressSource (who receives it)

     Implementation should still validate:
       IF multiZipJobs[i] uses zipRequestIdSource:
         THEN zipFilename MUST identify a zip file within that upload request.
       IF multiZipJobs[i] uses zipDocumentIdSource:
         THEN filename MUST exist inside the referenced zipDocumentId.

   jobTemplate scoping:
     Same as POST /static — a top-level jobTemplate provides defaults for all jobs
     in multiZipJobs, with each job item able to override it.
*)

submitMultiZipParams =
      docSourceZipFileRef
    + multiZipJobs
    + [ paymentDetails ]
    + [ tags ] ;


(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(* Endpoint: POST /batch/zip/address-capture                                            *)
(* @summary Submit ZIP batch — address capture *)
(* @description Submits a ZIP-based mailing batch where recipient addresses are captured externally. No inline recipient addresses are required. *)
(* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)

(* English meaning:
   - Zip-based submission where addresses are captured externally.
   - Body MAY include jobTemplate.
   - Body MUST include zipDocumentSource (zip-only; equivalent to docSourceZipFile).
   - Body MAY include paymentDetails, returnAddress, jobOptions, tags.
   - Body does NOT include recipientAddressSource because address capture occurs
     outside this JSON body.
*)

(* Decision / validation rules (implementation-required):
   Address capture constraint:
     IF request body includes recipientAddressSource (directly or nested)
       THEN reject.

   Zip-only constraint:
     zipDocumentSource is defined as:
       zipDocumentIdSource | zipRequestIdSource
     (equivalent to docSourceZipFile).

     So the schema already prevents non-zip variants. Implementation should still validate:
       - the zip exists / is accessible
       - zipFilename (for zipRequestIdSource) identifies a zip within the upload request
       - filename (for both zip modes where present) selects a real file inside the zip.

     IF using zipRequestIdSource:
       THEN zipFilename MUST identify a zip file within the upload request.
            filename (inner file) selection is not provided at top-level here,
            so processing MUST define how the server selects files/jobs from the zip
            (e.g., implicit enumeration, metadata inside zip, or subsequent capture step).

   Job list constraint:
     IF request body includes multiDocJobs OR multiZipJobs OR pdfSplitJobsWithAddress OR pdfSplitJobsNoAddress (i.e., any jobs array)
       THEN reject.

   jobTemplate vs jobOptions:
     Apply the same mutual-exclusion/default policy as /static.
*)

submitMultiZipAddressCaptureParams =
      [ jobTemplate ]
    + zipDocumentSource
    + [ paymentDetails ]
    + [ returnAddress ]
    + [ jobOptions ]
    + [ tags ] ;


(***********************************)
(*           CORE OBJECTS           *)
(***********************************)

(* @doc Saved job template name; pre-populates all print and mail options. Mutually exclusive with jobOptions. *)
jobTemplate = string ; (* @hint static standard_letter *)

(* @doc Optional sender return address printed on the mailpiece. *)
returnAddress =
      firstName + lastName
    + [ company ]
    + address1
    + city + state + zip + country
    + [ address2 ] + [ address3 ] ;

(* @doc Explicit print and mail configuration options. Mutually exclusive with jobTemplate. *)
jobOptions =
      documentClass
    + layout
    + productionTime
    + envelope
    + color
    + paperType
    + printOption
    + mailClass ;

(* @doc Document class determining the mailpiece format. *)
documentClass  = "letter" | "postcard" | "brochure" | "flat" ; (* @hint static letter *)
(* @doc Page layout controlling where the recipient address is printed. *)
layout         = "address_on_first_page" | "address_on_back_page" ; (* @hint static address_on_first_page *)
(* @doc Production time preference (next_day, two_day, etc.). *)
productionTime = "next_day" | "two_day" | "three_day" | "standard" | "same_day" ; (* @hint static next_day *)
(* @doc Envelope type used for the mailing. *)
envelope       = "standard" | "none" | "flat" | "double_window" ; (* @hint static standard *)
(* @doc Color mode for printing (full_color or black_and_white). *)
color          = "full_color" | "black_and_white" ; (* @hint static full_color *)
(* @doc Paper stock for printing. *)
paperType      = "white" | "white_24" | "ivory" | "glossy" ; (* @hint static white *)
(* @doc Duplex setting (double_sided or single_sided). *)
printOption    = "double_sided" | "single_sided" ; (* @hint static double_sided *)
(* @doc USPS mail class (first_class, standard, or non_profit). *)
mailClass      = "first_class" | "standard" | "non_profit" ; (* @hint static first_class *)

(* @doc Optional list of user-defined string tags for reporting and filtering. *)
tags = tagsList ;
(* @doc Array of user-defined string tags. *)
tagsList = { string } ;

(***********************************)
(*          ADDRESS OBJECTS         *)
(***********************************)

(* @doc Recipient's first name. *)
firstName = string ; (* @hint faker first_name *)
(* @doc Recipient's last name. *)
lastName  = string ; (* @hint faker last_name *)
(* @doc Recipient's company or organisation name (optional). *)
company   = string ; (* @hint faker company *)

(* @doc Primary street address line. *)
address1  = string ; (* @hint faker street_address *)
(* @doc Secondary address line (suite, apartment, floor, etc.). *)
address2  = string ; (* @hint static Suite 100 *)
(* @doc Tertiary address line. *)
address3  = string ; (* @hint static  *)

(* @doc City name. *)
city     = string ; (* @hint faker city *)
(* @doc Two-letter state or province abbreviation. *)
state    = string ; (* @hint faker state_abbr *)
(* @doc ZIP or postal code. *)
zip      = string ; (* @hint faker zipcode *)
(* @doc Country code (e.g. USA). *)
country  = string ; (* @hint static USA *)

(* @doc User-defined merge variable 1 — forwarded to the address list merge mapping for personalisation. *)
foo1 = string ; (* @hint static Custom Field 1 *)
(* @doc User-defined merge variable 2 — forwarded to the address list merge mapping for personalisation. *)
foo2 = string ; (* @hint static Custom Field 2 *)

(* @doc Mailing address with required core fields (name, address1, city, state, zip, country) and optional extended fields (company, address2, address3, foo1, foo2). *)
address =
      firstName + lastName
    + address1
    + city + state + zip + country
    + [ address2 ] + [ address3 ]
    + [ foo1 ] + [ foo2 ] ;

(* @doc Recipient address specification — one of: inline single address (with optional mapping), inline address list (with optional mapping), stored list ID, or stored address ID. *)
recipientAddressSource =
      singleAddress
    | recipientAddressByList
    | recipientAddressByAddressId
    | recipientAddressByListId ; (* @structural named_wrapper_oneof *)

(* @doc A single recipient mailing address (alias for address). *)
singleAddress = address ;

(* @doc Inline list of recipient addresses with an optional merge-field mapping ID. *)
recipientAddressByList =
    [ mappingId ] + addressList + [ addressListName ] ;

(* @doc Reference to a previously stored recipient address list by its integer ID. *)
recipientAddressByListId =
    addressListId ;

(* @doc Reference to a previously stored individual recipient address by its integer ID. *)
recipientAddressByAddressId =
    addressId ;

(* @doc Integer ID of a merge-field mapping profile that associates address columns to template variables. If omitted, the account default mapping is used. *)
mappingId = id ; (* @hint static 5001 *)
(* @doc Optional label for this recipient address record. *)
addressName = string ; (* @hint static Main Office *)
(* @doc Optional name for this address list record. *)
addressListName = string ; (* @hint static Marketing Campaign Q1 *)
(* @doc Integer ID of a previously stored recipient address list. *)
addressListId = id ; (* @hint static 1001 *)
(* @doc Integer ID of a previously stored individual recipient address. *)
addressId = id ; (* @hint static 2001 *)

(* @doc List of recipient mailing addresses — used for batch sends and mail merge. *)
addressList   = { address } ;

(***********************************)
(*        DOCUMENT SOURCE MODES     *)
(***********************************)

(* @doc Source a document by its previously stored document ID. *)
documentIdSource = documentId ; (* @structural single_field_wrapper *)
(* @doc Integer ID of a previously stored or uploaded document. *)
documentId = id ; (* @hint random_int 10000 99999 *)

(* @doc Source a document from a prior file upload by request ID. If the upload request contained multiple files, filename is required to identify which one. *)
requestIdSource = requestId + [ filename ] ;
(* @doc Integer ID of a prior file upload request. Also returned in success responses. *)
requestId = id ; (* @hint random_int 10000 99999 *)
(* @doc Filename of a specific file within an upload request or ZIP archive. *)
filename = string ; (* @hint static document.pdf *)

(* @doc Fetch the document from an external URL at submission time. *)
urlSource = url ; (* @structural single_field_wrapper *)
(* @doc URL from which the API will fetch the document at submission time. *)
url = string ; (* @hint static https://example.com/documents/sample.pdf *)

(* @doc Source a specific file within a stored ZIP archive — requires the archive ID and the filename of the target file within the archive. *)
zipDocumentIdSource = zipDocumentId + filename ;
(* @doc Integer ID of a previously stored ZIP archive. *)
zipDocumentId = id ; (* @hint random_int 10000 99999 *)

(* TO CHECK *)
(* @doc Source a specific file within an uploaded ZIP archive — requires the upload request ID, the zip filename within that request, and the target filename in the zip. *)
zipRequestIdSource = requestId + zipFilename + filename ;
(* @doc Filename of the ZIP file within an upload request (distinguishes the zip from other files uploaded in the same request). *)
zipFilename = string ; (* @hint static documents.zip *)

(* Zip file reference without filename - for multi/zip top-level *)
(* @doc Reference to a stored ZIP archive without a file selection — used at the batch job top level where individual job items select their own filenames. *)
zipDocumentIdOnly = zipDocumentId ; (* @structural single_field_wrapper *)
(* @doc Reference to an uploaded ZIP archive by request ID only — used at the batch top level; individual job items carry the filename selection. *)
zipRequestIdOnly = requestId ; (* @structural single_field_wrapper *)

(* @doc ZIP document source — either a stored zip archive (zipDocumentId) or an uploaded zip archive (requestId). *)
zipDocumentSource =
      zipDocumentIdSource
    | zipRequestIdSource ; (* @structural named_wrapper_oneof *)

(* Translator note:
   - docSourceStandard/docSourceZipFile/docSourceAll are specialized document source variants used to keep
     endpoint schemas tight (only accepting the source types each endpoint supports).
   - zipDocumentSource is used only by /batch/zip/address-capture and is intentionally zip-only.
   - Zip-only behavior for /batch/zip is enforced indirectly via multiZipJobItem using docSourceZipFile.
*)

(* @doc Document source — standard (non-zip) variants only: requestId, documentId, or URL. *)
docSourceStandard = documentIdSource | requestIdSource | urlSource ; (* @structural named_wrapper_oneof transparent_oneof_grouping *)
(* @doc Document source — zip variants: a specific file within a stored ZIP (zipDocumentId + filename) or uploaded ZIP (requestId + zipFilename + filename). *)
docSourceZipFile  = zipDocumentIdSource | zipRequestIdSource ; (* @structural named_wrapper_oneof transparent_oneof_grouping *)
(* @doc Top-level ZIP archive reference for batch endpoints — identifies the archive itself, not a file within it. No filename is required at this level. *)
docSourceZipFileRef = zipDocumentIdOnly | zipRequestIdOnly ;  (* For multi/zip top-level - zip reference without filename *) (* @structural named_wrapper_oneof *)
(* @doc Document source — accepts any supported variant: requestId, documentId, URL, or zip-based (zipDocumentId or zipRequestId). *)
docSourceAll      = docSourceStandard | docSourceZipFile ;

(***********************************)
(*           MERGE DOCUMENTS        *)
(***********************************)

(* @doc Ordered list of document references to merge into one output document (POST /mail-merge). *)
mergeDocumentSource = documentsToMerge ;
(* @doc Ordered array of document references to merge into one output document. Minimum two entries required. *)
documentsToMerge = { mergeDocumentRef } ;

(* @doc A single document to include in the merge — either a stored document ID or an upload request ID (with optional filename). *)
mergeDocumentRef =
      mergeByDocumentId
    | mergeByRequestId ; (* @structural named_wrapper_oneof *)

(* @doc Merge a stored document identified by its document ID. *)
mergeByDocumentId = documentId ; (* @structural single_field_wrapper *)
(* @doc Merge an uploaded document identified by its upload request ID, with an optional filename when the request contains multiple files. *)
mergeByRequestId  = requestId + [ filename ] ;

(***********************************)
(*              JOB LISTS           *)
(***********************************)

(* PLANNED — reserved for POST /static/multi (not yet implemented).
   multiDocJobs and multiDocJobItem schemas are generated but not wired to any endpoint path. *)
(* @doc List of independent document-per-recipient jobs (each job has its own document source and recipient address). *)
multiDocJobs = { multiDocJobItem } ;

(* @doc A single independent document job entry within a multi-doc batch. *)
multiDocJobItem =
      [ jobTemplate ]
    + docSourceAll
    + recipientAddressSource ;

(* @doc List of page-range job items, each with its own inline recipient address. *)
pdfSplitJobsWithAddress = { pdfSplitJobItemWithAddress } ;
(* @doc List of page-range job items without inline addresses — addresses are captured externally (POST /batch/split/address-capture). *)
pdfSplitJobsNoAddress   = { pdfSplitJobItemNoAddress } ;

(* @doc A single page-range job entry: page range (startPage, endPage) plus a recipient address. *)
pdfSplitJobItemWithAddress = [ jobTemplate ] + startPage + endPage + recipientAddressSource ;
(* @doc A single page-range job entry: page range only (no address — used for address-capture endpoint). *)
pdfSplitJobItemNoAddress   = [ jobTemplate ] + startPage + endPage ;

(* @doc First page of this job's page range, 1-indexed (inclusive). *)
startPage = integer ; (* @hint random_int 1 5 *)
(* @doc Last page of this job's page range (inclusive). Must be >= startPage. *)
endPage   = integer ; (* @hint random_int 6 10 *)

(* Zip-only jobs list:
   - Used by POST /batch/zip.
   - Zip file specified at top-level (docSourceZipFileRef in submitMultiZipParams).
   - Each item specifies optional jobTemplate, filename (which file within zip), and recipient.
   - Each job is independent with its own template and recipient.
*)
(* @doc List of per-file job items extracted from a ZIP archive (POST /batch/zip). *)
multiZipJobs = { multiZipJobItem } ;
(* @doc A single ZIP file job entry: optional job template, filename within the ZIP, and recipient address. *)
multiZipJobItem = [ jobTemplate ] + filename + recipientAddressSource ;

(***********************************)
(*           PRIMITIVE ALIASES      *)
(***********************************)

(* @doc Integer identifier — alias for integer, used for all ID fields. *)
id = integer ;

(********************************)
(*          PAYMENT DETAILS       *)
(********************************)

(* @doc Payment method — one of: creditCard, invoice, ACH bank transfer, or account credit. *)
paymentDetails =
      creditCardPayment
    | invoicePayment
    | achPayment
    | userCreditPayment
(*  | applePayPayment   -- commented out for initial testing *)
(*  | googlePayPayment  -- commented out for initial testing *)
    ;

(* @doc Credit card payment variant. *)
creditCardPayment =
      "creditCard"
    + creditCardDetails ;

(* @doc Invoice payment — billed to an existing account invoice. *)
invoicePayment =
      "invoice"
    + invoiceDetails ;

(* @doc ACH bank transfer payment variant. *)
achPayment =
      "ach"
    + achDetails ;

(* @doc Payment deducted from the account's prepaid credit balance. *)
userCreditPayment =
      "userCredit"
    + creditAmount ;

(*
applePayPayment =
      "applePay"
    + applePayDetails ;

googlePayPayment =
      "googlePay"
    + googlePayDetails ;
*)

(* @doc Credit card payment fields: card type, card number, expiration date, and CVV. *)
creditCardDetails =
      cardType
    + cardNumber
    + expirationDate
    + cvv ;

(* @doc Invoice payment fields: invoice number and amount due. *)
invoiceDetails =
      invoiceNumber
    + amountDue ;

(* @doc ACH payment fields: routing number, bank account number, and check digit. *)
achDetails =
      routingNumber
    + accountNumber
    + checkDigit ;

(* @doc Account credit payment fields: monetary amount and ISO currency code. *)
creditAmount =
      amount
    + currency ;

(* @doc ISO 4217 currency code (USD, EUR, GBP, CAD, or AUD). *)
currency = "USD" | "EUR" | "GBP" | "CAD" | "AUD" ;
(* @doc Monetary amount as a numeric value. *)
amount = number ;

(* @doc Credit card number (PAN) as a string. *)
cardNumber = string ; (* @hint static "4111111111111111" *)
(* @doc Card expiration date containing month and year. *)
expirationDate = month + year ;
(* @doc Expiration month as an integer (1-12). *)
month = integer ; (* @hint static 12 *)
(* @doc Expiration year as a four-digit integer (e.g. 2029). *)
year = integer ; (* @hint static 2029 *)
(* @doc Card security code (CVV/CVC) as an integer. *)
cvv = integer ; (* @hint static 123 *)
(* @doc ABA bank routing number. *)
routingNumber = string ; (* @hint aba_routing_number *)
(* @doc Bank account number. *)
accountNumber = string ; (* @hint static "1234567890" *)
(* @doc ACH check digit. *)
checkDigit = integer ;
(* @doc Invoice reference number. *)
invoiceNumber = string ;
(* @doc Amount due on the invoice. *)
amountDue = number ;

(* @doc Card brand enum: visa, mastercard, discover, or americanExpress. *)
cardType = "visa" | "mastercard" | "discover" | "americanExpress" ; (* @hint static visa *)

(********************************)
(*      APPLE PAY (TOKENIZED)       *)
(* Apple Pay definitions intentionally commented out for initial testing *)
(********************************)

